{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/d375-measure/packet-v10-1.md'","aggregated_output":"# Packet v10-1\n\n**The question:** What gross margin will NVIDIA report for FY2028?\n\nDue 2028-02-28. Possible answers:\n- 1 Strongly bullish: FY2028 gross margin is at least 75%.\n- 2 Bullish: FY2028 gross margin is at least 73% but below 75%.\n- 3 Neutral: FY2028 gross margin is at least 71% but below 73%.\n- 4 Bearish: FY2028 gross margin is at least 69% but below 71%.\n- 5 Strongly bearish: FY2028 gross margin is below 69%.\n\n**8 statements read on 2026-09-24:**\n\n- **v10-1-1** (stored attribution: fool.com (analyst)): The author calculates that Nvidia trades at less than 15 times next year's earnings and says this implies almost no growth is priced into the stock.\n  - Passage: \"At less than 15 times next year's earnings, Nvidia's stock has almost no growth priced into it today.\"\n- **v10-1-2** (stored attribution: AWS and NVIDIA): AWS and NVIDIA plan to build AI factories for the U.S. government, enabling delivery of 100,000 GPUs on AWS secure infrastructure for federal and national-security workloads.\n  - Passage: \"AWS and NVIDIA will build AI factories for the U.S. government, enabling the delivery of “100,000 GPUs on AWS’s secure infrastructure for federal and national-security workloads.”\"\n- **v10-1-3** (stored attribution: Jensen Huang): Nvidia CEO Jensen Huang said Nvidia’s chip sales would double next year; the item does not specify the sales measure or year.\n  - Passage: \"Huang, who said that Nvidia would double its chip sales next year\"\n- **v10-1-4** (stored attribution: Amazon Robotics and NVIDIA): Amazon Robotics plans to integrate NVIDIA’s full-stack physical AI platform into its robotics projects.\n  - Passage: \"On the physical AI side, Amazon Robotics will work with NVIDIA to integrate its full-stack physical AI platform, helping ramp up the development of Amazon’s robotics projects.\"\n- **v10-1-5** (stored attribution: fool.com (analyst)): The author estimates the five largest AI hyperscalers will spend nearly $800 billion on data centers in calendar 2026.\n  - Passage: \"Considering the big five AI hyperscalers will spend nearly $800 billion on data centers this year, that's huge growth still to come.\"\n- **v10-1-6** (stored attribution: AWS and NVIDIA): AWS and NVIDIA announced a plan to deploy 2 million additional NVIDIA GPUs across AWS infrastructure between 2027 and 2028.\n  - Passage: \"Now, the two powerhouses have announced a staggering expansion of this existing partnership which will, among other things — but this is certainly the standout headline — include the deployment of 2 million additional NVIDIA GPUs across AWS infrastructure between 2027 and 2028.\"\n- **v10-1-7** (stored attribution: Nvidia): The author says Nvidia estimates global data-center capital expenditures will reach $3 trillion–$4 trillion by 2030.\n  - Passage: \"Nvidia estimates that global data center capital expenditures will rise to between $3 trillion and $4 trillion by 2030.\"\n- **v10-1-8** (stored attribution: fool.com (analyst)): The author says Nvidia trades at 29 times trailing earnings.\n  - Passage: \"It trades for a very reasonable 29 times earnings.\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item\":\"v10-1-1\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The stock's earnings multiple does not give or revise NVIDIA's FY2028 gross margin.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v10-1-2\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The GPU delivery plan does not state a price, cost, or gross margin.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v10-1-3\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"A forecast of chip sales growth does not establish gross margin.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v10-1-4\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The robotics integration plan does not address NVIDIA's gross margin.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v10-1-5\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Hyperscaler data-center spending does not establish NVIDIA's gross margin.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v10-1-6\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The GPU deployment plan does not state the revenue or costs needed to assess gross margin.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v10-1-7\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"A global data-center spending estimate for 2030 does not establish NVIDIA's FY2028 gross margin.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v10-1-8\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The trailing earnings multiple does not address FY2028 gross margin.\"}\n{\"done\":true,\"items\":8}"}}
